# Local tooling scratch, not part of the design system.
.extract.py

# Local render-check artifacts. _ds_bundle.js is a stand-in for the bundle the
# Claude Design app generates itself -- regenerate with `node docs/build_bundle.js`.
# It must never be pushed, or it would clobber the real one.
_ds_bundle.js
.render/
.probe/

# Sub-agent scratch: probe pages and one-off screenshots.
.probe/
.vendor/

# Local overview page (docs/gen_gallery.py), built from .render/ screenshots above.
gallery.html

# Vendored copies of the Claude Design app's OWN css/js, fetched by URL when reverse-engineering
# its "Design System" pane styling. Same reasoning as .vendor/ above but for the app itself: its
# asset URLs are versioned build hashes (e.g. index-D0fefd-i.js) that rot the moment a new build
# ships, so anything read from them gets saved here rather than linked. Never a copy of a whole
# page we saved by hand (that's a one-off, not vendored) -- just fetched CSS/JS by URL.
.claude-design-vendor/

# A raw browser save of the Claude Design app. The pre-render SSR shell has none of the actual
# page's CSS or DOM (all client-rendered), so this is only ever useful as a "Webpage, Complete"
# save's html file, and even then it embeds the account's own email/org id in a JSON payload.
# Never push it.
claude-design.html
claude-design_files/
